    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of the lineup. His efficiency score of 79.74 is driven by a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Dean Kremer, where the platoon advantage provides a +14% lift to his base projection. While **Kyle Tucker** (63.91) and **Jacob Wilson** (66.55) also project as high-floor, reliable starters, **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the most likely candidate to provide the multi-category production\u2014specifically in Runs and SB potential\u2014that our Roto strategy demands. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.10) remains a lock despite the moderate toughness of Sonny Gray, as his ability to consistently contribute in HR and RBI keeps him in the daily rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimization engine centered on the final outfield spot and utility usage. **Wade Meckler** (42.35) fell just short of inclusion; despite his elite sprint speed, his projected matchup against MacKenzie Gore presents a difficult L/L platoon disadvantage that capped his efficiency. Consequently, the team will lean on the offensive depth of **Andy Pages** (60.44), whose efficiency benefits from a favorable lineup slot and stable matchup against Noah Cameron. Owners should monitor the 31% rain risk affecting **Drake Baldwin**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; while **Luis Robert Jr.** is a critical component of our SB pursuit, any weather-induced delay or postponement would significantly hamper our daily caps. While **Coby Mayo** (44.86) remains in the lineup due to thin alternatives, his low score suggests he is on the bubble and needs to capitalize on his limited opportunities to justify his roster spot.",
